  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There is a magician fighting against NNN cities. City iii has an army with a strength of AiA_iAi​.\n\nLet KKK denote the city where the magician is currently at.\n\nInitially, K=1K = 1K=1.\n\nEvery second, the magician can do **exactly one** of the following:\n\n\nIf K&lt;NK \\lt NK&lt;N, move to the (K+1)(K+1)(K+1)-th city and hence increase KKK by 111; **or**\nChoose an index i≤Ki \\leq Ki≤K and set AiA_iAi​ to 000, hence destroying the iii-th city's army.\n\nNote that this move does not change KKK.\nAfter the magician has made his move, every city will attack the magician, and he will take damage equal to the current sum of all the armies' strengths, that is, (A1+A2+…+AN)\\left(A_1 + A_2 + \\ldots + A_N\\right)(A1​+A2​+…+AN​).\n\nIf the magician chooses his moves optimally, find the minimum possible total damage he will take before every army is destroyed.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN — the number of cities.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible total damage the magician must take.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤50001 \\leq N \\leq 50001≤N≤5000",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 500050005000."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n5\n2\n1 3\n3\n3 2 1",
        "output": "0\n5\n8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Consider the following sequence of spells:\n\nChoose i=1i=1i=1 and set Ai=0A_i = 0Ai​=0.\nThe magician will now take 000 damage, and the process since every army has been destroyed.\n\nTest case 222: Consider the following sequence of spells:\n\nThe magician will move to city 222, so K=2K = 2K=2. The array remains A=[1,3]A = [1, 3]A=[1,3], so he will take 1+3=41+3 = 41+3=4 damage.\nChoose i=2i=2i=2 and set A2=0A_2 = 0A2​=0. The array is now [1,0][1, 0][1,0], so he will take 1+0=11+0 = 11+0=1 damage.\nChoose i=1i=1i=1 and set A1=0A_1 = 0A1​=0. The array is now [0,0][0, 0][0,0], so he will take 0+0=00+0 = 00+0=0 damage.\nAll armies have been destroyed, so the process ends.\n\nThe total damage taken is 4+1=54+1 = 54+1=5. It can be shown that this is the minimum possible."
      }
    ]
  },
